<title>POLAND: POLISH WHEAT/BARLEY PRICES SLIP, RYE UP LAST WEEK.</title>
<headline>POLISH WHEAT/BARLEY PRICES SLIP, RYE UP LAST WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Agriculture Ministry said in a statement wheat and barley prices eased while rye prices inched up during last week's grain auctions.</p>
<p>POLISH FARM AUCTION PRICES (AVERAGE)</p>
<p>  Product   week to April 12   previous week    yr/yr change</p>
<p>   Wheat	53.75 zl/q	 54.27 zl/q	 -16.0 pct</p>
<p>   Rye	  39.64 zl/q	 39.48 zl/q	   1.6 pct</p>
<p>   Barley     47.54 zl/q	 48.02 zl/q	 -15.0 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: zl/q = zlotys per quintal.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom+48 22 653 9700</p>
